<%- api_series = Marten::VERSION.split(".")[0..1].join(".") -%>
# Marten project guide for coding agents

<%- if context.edge -%>
This project uses Marten <%= Marten::VERSION %> from the development branch. Follow the guides at <https://martenframework.com/docs/next/> and the API reference at <https://martenframework.com/docs/api/dev/index.html>. The guide index is at <https://martenframework.com/docs/llms.txt>. The full text of those guides is at <https://martenframework.com/docs/llms-full.txt>.
<%- else -%>
This project uses Marten <%= Marten::VERSION %>. Follow the guides at <https://martenframework.com/docs/> and the API reference at <https://martenframework.com/docs/api/<%= api_series %>/index.html>. These guide URLs track the latest stable release. The API URL is pinned to <%= api_series %>. When a guide and that API disagree, follow the API.
<%- end -%>

Handlers process requests. Schemas validate input. Models persist records. Templates render HTML. Arrivals from Django or Rails should start with the concept maps linked below and use these names.

## Layout

- `config/settings/` — settings, including `installed_apps`
- `config/routes.cr` — routes
- `src/models/` — models
- `src/handlers/` — handlers
- `src/schemas/` — schemas
- `src/emails/` — emails
- `src/templates/` — templates
- `src/migrations/` — migrations
- `src/project.cr` — requires project code (`./models/**`, `./handlers/**`, `./schemas/**`, `./emails/**`)
- `src/cli.cr` — requires migrations (`./migrations/**`)
- `spec/` — specs

## Requires

`src/project.cr` requires `./emails/**`, `./handlers/**`, `./models/**`, and `./schemas/**`. A new file under one of those directories is compiled when its path matches the glob.

`src/cli.cr` requires `./project` and then `./migrations/**`. Migration files are compiled through `src/cli.cr`.

The `src/` tree is the main application. It is installed automatically and does not appear in `config.installed_apps`. An additional application must be listed in `config.installed_apps` in `config/settings/base.cr`, required from `src/project.cr`, and its CLI entry required from `src/cli.cr`. `marten gen app` makes those edits. An application added by hand needs the same ones.

## Commands

Prefer generators. Run `marten gen <name> --help` for options.

```bash
marten gen model Article title:string{128} author:many_to_one{User}
marten gen handler ArticleListHandler
marten gen schema ArticleSchema title:string body:string
marten gen email WelcomeEmail
marten gen app blog
marten genmigrations
marten migrate
crystal spec
marten serve
```

After a model change, run `marten genmigrations`, read the file it writes, then run `marten migrate`. `genmigrations` sees the main application and the applications listed in `installed_apps`. Create a custom migration with `marten genmigrations <app> --empty`.

## Requests

Define routes in `config/routes.cr` with `path`. Prefer a generic handler when the handler lists, shows, creates, updates, or deletes a record.

CSRF protection is enabled. A form that submits `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, or `DELETE` includes `{% csrf_input %}`. Any other unsafe request sends the token in the `X-CSRF-Token` header.

## Specs

`spec/spec_helper.cr` sets `MARTEN_ENV=test` and requires `marten/spec`. Spec files require that helper.

`crystal spec` compiles the project before running examples. While iterating, pass one file:

```bash
crystal spec spec/models/article_spec.cr
```

